LONG5.push(
 {t:'Ruth Asawa: Shapes from Wire',k:'Article',p:[
  'Ruth Asawa was born in California in 1926. Her family were farmers, and as a girl she drew pictures in the dirt with her feet while she worked in the fields.',
  'During World War II, Ruth and her family were forced to leave their home and live in camps with other Japanese Americans. In the camps, she met artists who taught her to draw.',
  'Later, on a trip to Mexico, Ruth watched people weave baskets from wire. She began to crochet wire into looping shapes that looked like floating clouds or sea creatures.',
  'Many people at first said her sculptures were "just crafts." Ruth kept working anyway. Today, her art hangs in major museums, and San Francisco named a school after her.',
  'Ruth also believed every child should be able to make art. She helped start art programs in public schools so students could learn from real artists.'],
  q:[['mc','What is the main idea of the article?','Ruth Asawa overcame hard times to become an important artist who also helped children make art.',['Wire is easy to bend.','Ruth Asawa learned to weave wire in Mexico.','Museums only show paintings.'],'What is the whole article about?','It tells <b>how Ruth Asawa became an artist and helped others</b>.'],
     ['ab','<b>Part A:</b> Which word best describes Ruth Asawa?','determined',['careless','jealous','shy'],'<b>Part B:</b> Which sentence best supports your answer in Part A?','Ruth kept working anyway.',['Ruth Asawa was born in California in 1926.','Her family were farmers.','She began to crochet wire into looping shapes.'],'What did she do when people doubted her?','She did not give up: <b>Ruth kept working anyway</b>.'],
     ['two','Which <b>two</b> events helped Ruth learn about art?',['She met artists in the camps who taught her to draw.','She watched people weave baskets from wire in Mexico.'],['She worked in the fields.','San Francisco named a school after her.','People called her art "just crafts."'],'Look for where she learned.','She learned from <b>artists in the camps</b> and from <b>wire basket weavers</b>.'],
     ['hl','Tap the sentence that shows how Ruth helped other children.','She helped start art programs in public schools','Look at the last paragraph.','<b>She helped start art programs in public schools</b>.'],
     ['mc','How is the article mostly organized?','in time order, from Ruth\'s childhood to later in her life',['as a list of opinions','as a comparison of two artists','as steps to make a sculpture'],'Look at the beginning of each paragraph.','It follows her life <b>in time order</b>.']]},
 {t:'The Stormy Crossing (a story told by Leo)',k:'Story',p:[
  'My little sister, Gaby, had never been on a boat, so when Dad said we would take the ferry to the island, she bounced all the way to the dock.',
  'Halfway across, the sky turned the color of an old bruise. Waves slapped the side of the ferry, and Gaby grabbed my arm so hard it hurt.',
  'I was scared too, but I remembered what Grandpa always said: "When the sea gets loud, make your voice calm." So I told Gaby stories about the dolphins we might see.',
  'By the time the island appeared through the rain, Gaby was laughing at my silly dolphin voices. Dad winked at me.',
  'That night, Gaby told Mom that the storm was the best part of the trip. I didn\'t tell her how fast my own heart had been beating.'],
  q:[['mc','Who is telling the story?','Leo, Gaby\'s older brother',['Gaby','Dad','Grandpa'],'Look at the title and the word "my".','The narrator is <b>Leo</b>, telling it in first person.'],
     ['ab','<b>Part A:</b> How does Leo feel during the storm?','scared, but he stays calm for his sister',['bored','angry at Dad','excited the whole time'],'<b>Part B:</b> Which sentence best supports your answer in Part A?','I was scared too, but I remembered what Grandpa always said: "When the sea gets loud, make your voice calm."',['My little sister, Gaby, had never been on a boat.','Dad winked at me.','By the time the island appeared through the rain, Gaby was laughing.'],'Look at paragraph 3.','He was <b>scared too</b> but used Grandpa\'s advice to stay calm.'],
     ['mc','What does the phrase "the color of an old bruise" describe?','a dark, purple-gray stormy sky',['Gaby\'s arm','the ferry','a sunset'],'What turned that color?','It describes the <b>dark stormy sky</b>.'],
     ['hl','Tap the sentence that shows Leo hid his own fear from Gaby.','I didn\'t tell her how fast my own heart had been beating.','Look at the last paragraph.','<b>He didn\'t tell her</b> how scared he had been.'],
     ['mc','How would the story be different if Gaby told it?','Readers might not know Leo was scared.',['There would be no storm.','Dad would be the main character.','Readers would learn more about the ferry.'],'What does only Leo know?','Only Leo knows his heart was racing, so <b>Gaby might not know he was scared</b>.']]}
);
